    <programlisting>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#<sp/>BVH2D<sp/>Spatial<sp/>Indexing<sp/>for<sp/>Path<sp/>SDF<sp/>Computation</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>document<sp/>records<sp/>the<sp/>performance<sp/>investigation<sp/>and<sp/>implementation<sp/>findings<sp/>for<sp/>accelerating<sp/>2D<sp/>Path<sp/>Signed<sp/>Distance<sp/>Field<sp/>(SDF)<sp/>evaluation<sp/>using<sp/>a<sp/>Bounding<sp/>Volume<sp/>Hierarchy<sp/>(`BVH2D`).</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>1.<sp/>Context<sp/>and<sp/>Motivation</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Computing<sp/>the<sp/>distance<sp/>field<sp/>of<sp/>a<sp/>2D<sp/>polyline<sp/>or<sp/>polygon<sp/>across<sp/>a<sp/>discrete<sp/>heightmap<sp/>grid<sp/>is<sp/>a<sp/>recurring<sp/>operation<sp/>in<sp/>terrain<sp/>authoring,<sp/>hydrology<sp/>(riverbed<sp/>carve<sp/>profiles),<sp/>and<sp/>carving<sp/>workflows.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>original<sp/>evaluation<sp/>in<sp/>`path_sdf_to_array`<sp/>and<sp/>`sdf_2d_polyline`<sp/>performed<sp/>brute-force<sp/>distance<sp/>evaluation:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>For<sp/>every<sp/>pixel<sp/>$(i,<sp/>j)$<sp/>in<sp/>a<sp/>$W<sp/>\times<sp/>H$<sp/>array,<sp/>iterate<sp/>across<sp/>all<sp/>$N$<sp/>path<sp/>segments.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Complexity:<sp/>$\mathcal{O}(W<sp/>\cdot<sp/>H<sp/>\cdot<sp/>N)$.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">For<sp/>dense<sp/>or<sp/>detailed<sp/>paths<sp/>($N<sp/>\ge<sp/>100$)<sp/>and<sp/>high-resolution<sp/>heightmaps<sp/>($512<sp/>\times<sp/>512$<sp/>or<sp/>higher),<sp/>this<sp/>approach<sp/>causes<sp/>significant<sp/>CPU<sp/>bottlenecks.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">HighMap<sp/>provides<sp/>an<sp/>internal<sp/>2D<sp/>Axis-Aligned<sp/>Bounding<sp/>Box<sp/>tree<sp/>(`hmap::BVH2D`).<sp/>By<sp/>indexing<sp/>the<sp/>segment<sp/>set<sp/>into<sp/>a<sp/>BVH,<sp/>the<sp/>nearest<sp/>segment<sp/>search<sp/>per<sp/>pixel<sp/>is<sp/>accelerated<sp/>via<sp/>branch-and-bound<sp/>pruning.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>2.<sp/>Algorithmic<sp/>Approach</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">###<sp/>Segment<sp/>Indexing</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Path<sp/>segments<sp/>$[p_k,<sp/>p_{k+1}]$<sp/>are<sp/>packaged<sp/>into<sp/>`Segment2D`<sp/>structs<sp/>storing<sp/>directional<sp/>vector<sp/>$d<sp/>=<sp/>p_{k+1}<sp/>-<sp/>p_k$<sp/>and<sp/>inverse<sp/>squared<sp/>length<sp/>$\frac{1}{\|d\|^2}$.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">A<sp/>`BVH2D`<sp/>tree<sp/>is<sp/>built<sp/>over<sp/>the<sp/>segments<sp/>in<sp/>$\mathcal{O}(N<sp/>\log<sp/>N)$<sp/>time.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">###<sp/>Branch-and-Bound<sp/>Distance<sp/>Query</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">For<sp/>a<sp/>given<sp/>query<sp/>point<sp/>$p<sp/>=<sp/>(x,<sp/>y)$:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">1.<sp/>Traverse<sp/>the<sp/>BVH<sp/>using<sp/>a<sp/>fixed-capacity<sp/>traversal<sp/>stack.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">2.<sp/>At<sp/>each<sp/>node,<sp/>compute<sp/>the<sp/>minimum<sp/>squared<sp/>distance<sp/>from<sp/>$p$<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>node&apos;s<sp/>axis-aligned<sp/>bounding<sp/>box<sp/>(`AABB2D`):</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/>$$d_{\text{box}}^2(p,<sp/>\text{box})<sp/>=<sp/>\max(0,<sp/>\text{box.min}_x<sp/>-<sp/>p_x,<sp/>p_x<sp/>-<sp/>\text{box.max}_x)^2<sp/>+<sp/>\max(0,<sp/>\text{box.min}_y<sp/>-<sp/>p_y,<sp/>p_y<sp/>-<sp/>\text{box.max}_y)^2$$</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">3.<sp/>If<sp/>$d_{\text{box}}^2<sp/>\ge<sp/>d_{\text{best}}^2$,<sp/>the<sp/>node<sp/>and<sp/>all<sp/>its<sp/>descendants<sp/>are<sp/>pruned.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">4.<sp/>For<sp/>internal<sp/>nodes,<sp/>visit<sp/>the<sp/>closer<sp/>child<sp/>first<sp/>to<sp/>tighten<sp/>$d_{\text{best}}^2$<sp/>quickly.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">5.<sp/>In<sp/>leaf<sp/>nodes,<sp/>evaluate<sp/>exact<sp/>point-to-segment<sp/>distance<sp/>squared<sp/>and<sp/>update<sp/>$d_{\text{best}}^2$.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Average<sp/>per-query<sp/>complexity<sp/>drops<sp/>to<sp/>$\mathcal{O}(\log<sp/>N)$,<sp/>reducing<sp/>overall<sp/>runtime<sp/>to<sp/>$\mathcal{O}(W<sp/>\cdot<sp/>H<sp/>\log<sp/>N)$.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">###<sp/>Support<sp/>for<sp/>Domain<sp/>Warping<sp/>and<sp/>Path<sp/>Closure</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>**Domain<sp/>Warping**:<sp/>Per-pixel<sp/>noise<sp/>displacements<sp/>(`p_noise_x`,<sp/>`p_noise_y`)<sp/>warp<sp/>coordinate<sp/>$p<sp/>=<sp/>(x<sp/>+<sp/>dx,<sp/>y<sp/>+<sp/>dy)$<sp/>before<sp/>querying<sp/>the<sp/>tree.<sp/>The<sp/>tree<sp/>does<sp/>not<sp/>require<sp/>reconstruction.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>**Closed<sp/>Paths**:<sp/>When<sp/>`path.is_closed()<sp/>==<sp/>true`,<sp/>the<sp/>closing<sp/>segment<sp/>is<sp/>included<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>BVH,<sp/>and<sp/>an<sp/>orientation/winding<sp/>sign<sp/>test<sp/>determines<sp/>interior<sp/>vs.<sp/>exterior<sp/>distances.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>3.<sp/>Benchmark<sp/>Measurements</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Google<sp/>Benchmark<sp/>was<sp/>executed<sp/>comparing<sp/>the<sp/>baseline<sp/>brute-force<sp/>approach<sp/>against<sp/>the<sp/>BVH<sp/>approach<sp/>on<sp/>a<sp/>CPU<sp/>with<sp/>6<sp/>physical<sp/>cores<sp/>(12<sp/>threads).</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
